  partName: Exhaust Manifold
  description: The Exhaust Manifold, located at the middle-center-rear of the engine,
    is a medium-sized, elongated, accent-yellow component that collects and directs
    exhaust gases away from the engine. Its elongated shape and accent-yellow color
    allow for efficient exhaust gas flow and easy identification during maintenance.
    Interestingly, the Exhaust Manifold's position at the rear of the engine enables
    it to work in conjunction with the Turbine Housing to optimize engine performance.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 0}
